<%# Two-column form section. On lg the title and description take the left
    third and the fields the right two thirds; below lg they stack. Sibling
    sections are split by an ink-150 hairline, so a form is one sv-card (p-6)
    holding a run of sections followed by shared/form_footer.
    The field column is a size container: grids inside it use container
    variants (@sm:grid-cols-2, @xl:grid-cols-3) so they follow the width the
    column really has, not the viewport (beside the sidebar on lg it is
    narrower than on a stacked tablet layout).
    Usage:
      render "shared/form_section", title: "Contato", description: "Opcional." do
        ...fields...
      end
    Locals:
      title        the section heading (h2, 15px semibold).
      description  optional 13px ink-600 text under the title.
      heading_id   optional id for the h2 (the section is labelled by it);
                   defaults to one derived from the title. %>
<%# locals: (title:, description: nil, heading_id: nil) -%>
<% heading_id ||= "secao-#{title.parameterize}" %>
<section class="grid gap-x-8 gap-y-5 border-t border-ink-150 py-6 first-of-type:border-t-0 first-of-type:pt-0 last-of-type:pb-0 lg:grid-cols-3"
         aria-labelledby="<%= heading_id %>">
  <div class="lg:col-span-1">
    <h2 id="<%= heading_id %>" class="text-[15px]/6 font-semibold text-ink-950"><%= title %></h2>
    <% if description.present? %>
      <p class="mt-1 max-w-prose text-[13px]/5 text-ink-600"><%= description %></p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <div class="@container min-w-0 space-y-5 lg:col-span-2">
    <%= yield %>
  </div>
</section>
